    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d492">

                <pb facs="0510" n="426" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp02/pg426"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. No. 763.72112/5633</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Saloniki</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Horton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Saloniki</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-11-22T18:00:00+02:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 22, 1917, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received November 23, 2.45
                        a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Does the Government of the United States approve American firms having business
                    relations with local firms on the English-French black list as having Austrian,
                    Bulgarian, or Turkish connections? If not, what advice can I give them as to
                    avoiding existing contracts whose fulfillment subjects American companies to
                    repressive measures of English and French authorities?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Horton</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
